IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `era-types`
IMPORT `era-periods`
IMPORT `era-notice`
IMPORT `era-unfair-dismissal`
IMPORT `era-redundancy`

-- Employment Rights Act 1996 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "An employee's contract has ended. What notice did the Act require; can
--    they complain of unfair dismissal, and by when; what is the basic
--    award; and are they entitled to a redundancy payment, and how much?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Dismissal case` HAS
    `the employee`                                      IS AN `Employee`
    `the termination`                                   IS A `Termination`
    `the unfair dismissal facts`                        IS AN `Unfair dismissal facts`
    `the redundancy facts`                              IS A `Redundancy facts`

DECLARE `Dismissal position` HAS
    `weeks of notice the employer had to give`          IS A NUMBER
    `weeks of notice the employee had to give`          IS A NUMBER
    `effective date of termination`                     IS A DATE
    `effective date of termination for ss 108 and 119`  IS A DATE
    `is dismissed`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `meets the unfair dismissal qualifying period`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `last day to present an unfair dismissal complaint` IS A DATE
    `basic award`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `entitled to a redundancy payment`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `redundancy payment`                                IS A NUMBER
    `last day of the s 164(1) period`                   IS A DATE

@ref ss 86, 95, 97, 108, 111, 119-122, 135-164, 207B, 211, 227
@export default The position under the Employment Rights Act 1996 (UK) when an employee's contract has ended: the statutory minimum notice each side had to give (s 86, on the material date); the effective date of termination (s 97(1)) and the later date for ss 108 and 119 (s 97(2), (4)); whether the employee was dismissed and meets the two-year qualifying period for unfair dismissal (s 108); the last day to present an unfair dismissal complaint (s 111(2)(a) with s 207B); the basic award if the tribunal may consider the complaint and finds the dismissal unfair (ss 119-122, 0 otherwise); whether the employee is entitled to a redundancy payment (ss 135-164) and its amount (s 162, 0 if not entitled); and the last day of the s 164(1) claim period. A week's pay is capped at £751 (s 227). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Dismissal case`  @desc The employee (date of birth, start of continuous employment, a week's pay), how and when the contract ended, the unfair dismissal facts and findings, and the redundancy facts and claim dates
GIVETH A `Dismissal position`
`the dismissal position for` c MEANS
    `Dismissal position` WITH
        `weeks of notice the employer had to give`          IS `the notice in weeks the employer must give` emp `on` material
        `weeks of notice the employee had to give`          IS `the notice in weeks the employee must give` emp `on` material
        `effective date of termination`                     IS `the effective date of termination under s 97(1) of` t
        `effective date of termination for ss 108 and 119`  IS `the effective date of termination for ss 108(1) and 119(1) of` emp `and` t
        `is dismissed`                                      IS `the employee is dismissed under s 95(1) by` t
        `meets the unfair dismissal qualifying period`      IS `the qualifying period in s 108 is met by` emp `for` t `with` u
        `last day to present an unfair dismissal complaint` IS `the last day to present an unfair dismissal complaint for` t `with` u
        `basic award`                                       IS `the basic award awarded to` emp `for` t `with` u
        `entitled to a redundancy payment`                  IS entitled
        `redundancy payment`                                IS IF entitled THEN `the amount of a redundancy payment under s 162 for` emp `and` t ELSE 0
        `last day of the s 164(1) period`                   IS `the last day of the s 164(1) period for` t
    WHERE
        emp      MEANS c's `the employee`
        t        MEANS c's `the termination`
        u        MEANS c's `the unfair dismissal facts`
        r        MEANS c's `the redundancy facts`
        material MEANS `the material date of` t
        entitled MEANS `is entitled to a redundancy payment` emp `for` t `with` r
